Source: gitcha
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Maintainer: inputloop <nathanielfrankford@gmail.com>
# npm fetches the server's dependencies from the committed lockfile at build time (network, or a filled npm cache).
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), nodejs (>= 20), npm
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/inputloop/gitcha
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/inputloop/gitcha.git
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: inputloop-gitcha
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, nodejs (>= 20), git, adduser
# ${gitcha:Recommends} is "cassandra" unless built with the pkg.gitcha.nocassandra profile.
Recommends: ${gitcha:Recommends}, gnupg, openssh-server, caddy
Description: Gitcha: forge, registry, hosting and community for inputloop
 Self-hosted packages, git repositories (HTTPS and SSH), static sites with
 custom domains, CI and lambda functions run by separate runners, billing with
 Stripe and PayPal, agents and Second Reader reviews, a social crawl, and
 operations tickets.  Every account uses a password and an authenticator app.
 .
 Its database lives in Apache Cassandra or in one file.  debconf asks for the
 settings, so a preseed file can install many servers unattended.  It starts
 only when that is asked for.

Package: inputloop-gitcha-runner
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, nodejs (>= 20), adduser
Recommends: bcontain
Description: Gitcha runner: CI jobs and functions in bContain VMs
 Registers with a Gitcha server, takes jobs, runs each in its own throwaway
 bContain VM, streams the log back and reports the result.  debconf can take
 the server and a registration token, so a preseed file registers it
 unattended.  It starts only when that is asked for.

Package: inputloop-gitcha-medic
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, nodejs (>= 20), inputloop-gitcha, bsdutils
Recommends: curl
Description: Gitcha medic: diagnose Gitcha, its Cassandra and its proxy, and mend what is safe
 Every five minutes (a timer) and by hand, looks at the Gitcha server on this
 machine, the Apache Cassandra node it keeps its database in and the nginx or
 Caddy in front; says in plain words what is wrong and why; runs the remedies
 that are safe to run unasked when told it may; parks the rest for a person
 (sudo gitcha-medic --yes NAME); and tells syslog and the rooms it is given
 (Tavern, chadgram, a webhook, a C4 folder).  An AI agent (the Claude API; a
 local model and inputloop's own agents are reserved names) can be asked for a
 second opinion over redacted facts; it cannot say yes for a person.

Package: inputloop-gitcha-omni-gateway
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, nodejs (>= 20)
Recommends: nginx, inputloop-tavern
Suggests: python3
Description: Omni gateway: your MCP servers behind HTTP, one token each, for Claude in a cloud sandbox
 Puts the stdio MCP servers named in /etc/inputloop/omni/members.json
 (vibrobeast's memory seat and persona sheets, Tavern, Gitcha) behind HTTP on
 loopback, one URL and one bearer token per member, each run as the user whose
 files it serves; nginx with TLS goes in front.  A Claude session in a cloud
 sandbox reaches them through the omni plugin (the hub, also here) or as remote
 MCP servers.  It starts only when that is asked for.
